# Flutter UI architecture

- Keep `Provider` and `ChangeNotifierProvider` as the app's state-management mechanism during UI work.
- Preserve `AuthGate` as the authentication boundary and its stream-driven signed-in/signed-out flow.
- Keep services injected through constructors or the existing provider setup; do not instantiate production services inside UI widgets.
- Preserve the interfaces and injected implementations for authentication, chat, and game persistence.
- Read and watch providers with the existing `context.read`, `context.watch`, `Consumer`, and `Provider.of` patterns as appropriate.
- Keep game-state loading and authentication orchestration outside purely presentational widgets.
- UI-only changes must not replace navigation, state management, service wiring, or startup behavior.
- Do not introduce Riverpod or `go_router` for UI changes.
- Prefer focused widget extraction without moving business logic into the widget tree.
